### b Some(Sysop)
B <user> — block / unblock user
Prefix + to force-block, - to force-unblock, or omit to toggle.
Hides their messages from you.
### profile Some(Sysop)
PROFILE — edit your display name
### passwd Some(Sysop)
PASSWD — change your password
You'll be asked for your current password, then the new one twice.
### stop Some(Sysop)
STOP — stop pending messages
### v Some(Sysop)
V — validate pending users
Enters the user validation workflow.
### pending Some(Sysop)
PENDING — list users awaiting validation
### .er Some(Sysop)
.ER — edit current room
Edit name, description, read-only flag, or min permission level.
### .eu Some(Sysop)
.EU <user> — edit a user's profile or permissions
Aides cannot promote to Sysop.
### ban Some(Sysop)
BAN <user> — ban a user account
### timeout Some(Sysop)
TIMEOUT <user> <days> — suspend a user account for 1-5 days
Logs them out immediately and rejects login with the days remaining shown; reactivates automatically once the timeout elapses. UNBAN lifts it early.
### u Some(Sysop)
U — list active user accounts
U banned — list banned accounts
U all — list all accounts (sysop)
### users Some(Sysop)
Users:
U         list active
U banned  list banned
U all     list all
SEARCH <q> find
WHOIS <u> details
### whois Some(Sysop)
WHOIS <user> — show account details
Includes level, status, join date, last login, and active sessions.
### unban Some(Sysop)
UNBAN <user> — lift a ban
### .aide Some(Sysop)
.AIDE/.SYSOP/.USER <user> — set a user's permission level
Promote a validated user to Aide or Sysop, or demote to User.
Validate pending users with V first.
### .sysop Some(Sysop)
.AIDE/.SYSOP/.USER <user> — set a user's permission level
Promote a validated user to Aide or Sysop, or demote to User.
Validate pending users with V first.
### .user Some(Sysop)
.AIDE/.SYSOP/.USER <user> — set a user's permission level
Promote a validated user to Aide or Sysop, or demote to User.
Validate pending users with V first.
### .c Some(Sysop)
.C — create a new room
Enters the room creation workflow.
### .dr Some(Sysop)
.DR <name> — delete a room
### .du Some(Sysop)
.DU <user> — soft-delete a user account
Sets status to deleted and ends active sessions.
### .pw Some(Sysop)
.PW <user> — reset a user to a single-use temp password
Returns a temp password to share; they must change it at next login.
### openaccess Some(Sysop)
OPENACCESS — disable verification requirement (SHTF mode)
All registrations immediately receive User-level access.
Takes effect immediately and persists to config.toml.
### closeaccess Some(Sysop)
CLOSEACCESS — restore verification requirement
New accounts must be validated by an aide or sysop.
Takes effect immediately and persists to config.toml.
### guestroom Some(Sysop)
GUESTROOM <name> — set guest room (created if needed)
Unverified users are placed here and cannot leave.
GUESTROOM OFF to disable.
Takes effect immediately and persists to config.toml.
### nothing-like-this Some(Sysop)
No help for 'nothing-like-this'.
H for commands, H reading/posting/navigation/account for topics.
### reading-mode
Reading mode:
F  next message
R  previous message
J <#>  jump to message
E  reply to this message
D  delete message
H  this help
X  exit reading
